  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "New models predict irAE risk, pediatric brain tumor survival and immunotherapy response from scRNA-seq, methylation and immune-state inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread links high-dimensional molecular profiles to clinical endpoints. irAEGIS applies a pathway-guided, interpretable hierarchical model to pre-treatment scRNA-seq to predict immune-related adverse event risk, outperforming seven comparators. MANTIS trains a neural network on genome-wide DNA methylation from 2,786 patients to predict time-dependent survival and treatment effects in childhood brain tumors. Genialis reports that a biology-first model inferring tumor immune state predicts immunotherapy response comparably to outcome-trained signatures. Resources supply the substrate: CALM pairs single-cell and bulk AML data with clinical annotations, DiseaseCIO maps multi-omics to intervention outcomes across 94 disease states, and RNAactDrug 2.0 connects RNA, CNV, mutation, methylation and enhancer features to drug sensitivity. A secondary strand addresses inference reliability. RIFTT and a 569,640-chimeric-RNA atlas with dependency screening tackle fusion detection. OncoSpot simulates Visium-like data with known subclones and CNAs. SpatioCAD reduces false positives in spatially variable gene detection. XenoMix quantifies mouse content in PDX methylation data, and flashscenic accelerates SCENIC 12-27x.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
